{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hello, Hana. Good to see you. Let me just confirm. Full name and date of birth.",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 4.88
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Hana Kobayashi, July 3, 1997.",
   "start": 5.97,
   "end": 8.93
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thank you. Last time you mentioned you were thinking about getting a dog. Did it happen?",
   "start": 10.13,
   "end": 14.01
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "It did. A little Shiba puppy. She's chewed two pairs of my shoes already.",
   "start": 15.24,
   "end": 19.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's the price of admission. So, how has your mood been since July?",
   "start": 19.72,
   "end": 23.42
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Honestly, really steady. On my mood chart app most days are a 5 or a 6. No big lows, no highs.",
   "start": 24.1,
   "end": 30.54
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "No stretches of feeling revved up, needing less sleep, spending more than usual.",
   "start": 31.38,
   "end": 35.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, the last time that happened was two years ago, before we found the right dose.",
   "start": 36.14,
   "end": 40.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And any low periods, losing interest in things, staying in bed.",
   "start": 41.12,
   "end": 44.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, not since last winter, and that was mild.",
   "start": 45.52,
   "end": 48.0
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How are you sleeping?",
   "start": 48.96,
   "end": 49.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "About seven hours, pretty regular. I keep the same bedtime, like you told me.",
   "start": 50.98,
   "end": 55.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good, you're on lamitrogen 200 milligrams once a day, correct.",
   "start": 56.38,
   "end": 60.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, well wait, is it 150? No, no, it's 200. The 150 was before the last increase.",
   "start": 61.4,
   "end": 68.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Right, 200, any missed doses.",
   "start": 68.92,
   "end": 70.96
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Maybe once a month I forget, then I just take it the next day as usual.",
   "start": 72.16,
   "end": 75.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's fine, any rash, mouth sores, or blisters anywhere.",
   "start": 76.44,
   "end": 79.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, nothing like that.",
   "start": 79.97,
   "end": 82.21
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Anything else you're taking.",
   "start": 82.71,
   "end": 83.95
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Just a multivitamin every morning. Oh, and that's actually what I wanted to ask about. My gynaecologist, Dr. Alvarez, wants to start me on birth control pills next month. The combination one, norgestimate and ethanol estradiol.",
   "start": 84.91,
   "end": 99.57
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'm glad you asked, that's important. The estrogen in combination pills can lower lamitrogen levels in your blood, sometimes by about half, so the dose that works now could stop being enough.",
   "start": 100.13,
   "end": 110.41
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Oh, I didn't know that.",
   "start": 111.21,
   "end": 112.11
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Most people don't, before we talk plans, any thoughts of suicide or of hurting yourself.",
   "start": 112.59,
   "end": 117.41
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, none. I still have my safety plan and 988 saved in my phone.",
   "start": 118.15,
   "end": 122.97
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good and I looked at your lab work from your primary care doctor in August. Your liver and kidney tests were all normal. Your blood pressure today is 112 over 70 and your weight is 131 same as last time. You're bright and relaxed today, mood euthemic, speech is normal, not pressured, and your thoughts are organized.",
   "start": 123.71,
   "end": 141.03
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "My brother takes lamatrogen for his seizures, actually, he never mentioned this.",
   "start": 141.91,
   "end": 146.37
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "It applies to anyone on it, so to sum up, your bipolar roman 2 disorder is stable on lamatrogen 200 milligrams a day, and we'll keep that dose for now. Here's the plan for the pill. I'd like a baseline lamatrogen level this week, drawn in the morning before your dose at our lab at 2200 Kessler Boulevard. Then once you start the pill, we'll recheck the level two to three weeks later, and I'll probably need to increase your dose.",
   "start": 146.83,
   "end": 168.41
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, and if I didn't want to deal with that.",
   "start": 169.47,
   "end": 171.29
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "A Progestin -only option or an IUD wouldn't really affect it. That's worth raising with Dr. Alvarez. Either way is fine with me, just keep me in the loop.",
   "start": 171.87,
   "end": 180.55
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I'll talk to her.",
   "start": 181.3,
   "end": 182.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Two safety reminders. If you ever get a rash, especially with fever or mouth sores, stop the lamitrogen and call us or go to the emergency room. And if you miss five days or more in a row, don't restart at 200, call us, because we need to build back up slowly.",
   "start": 182.82,
   "end": 197.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Got it.",
   "start": 197.92,
   "end": 198.34
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Keep the multivitamin. I'll see you in three months, unless the level or the pill changes things sooner. Is 317 -555 -0172 still the best number for the lab results?",
   "start": 198.76,
   "end": 210.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yep, same number. Thanks, Dr. Petrenko.",
   "start": 211.44,
   "end": 213.88
  }
 ],
